{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDE5LzAwL011cmRlciUyMEluJTIwVGhlJTIwRnJvbnQlMjBSb3clMjBUaGUlMjBTYW4lMjBGcmFuY2lzY28lMjBCYXklMjBBcmVhJTIwVGhyYXNoJTIwTWV0YWwlMjBTdG9yeSUyMCUyODIwMTklMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Murder In The Front Row The San Francisco Bay Area Thrash Metal Story","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/lsVmolhCxoR10YRrJIltTjZTVZt.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/o5hxa4ES8a2esehZMhqBnntAlIr.jpg","description":"Murder In The Front Row: The San Francisco Bay Area Thrash Metal Story. In the early 1980’s, a small group of dedicated Bay Area headbangers shunned the hard rock of MTV and Hollywood hairspray bands in favor of a more dangerous brand of metal that became known as thrash! From the tape trading network to the clubs to the record stores and fanzines, director Adam Dubin reveals how the scene nurtured the music and the music spawned a movement.  Murder In The Front Row is told through powerful first person testimony and stunning animation and photography. The film is a social study of a group of young people defying the odds and building something essential for themselves.  Featuring interviews with Metallica, Megadeth, Slayer, Anthrax, Exodus, Testament, Death Angel, Possessed and many more! Narrated by Brian Posehn.\n\nReleased 31 May 2019 · United States of America · Language: English · 92 min\nStudio: Bonded By Blood\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2019","genres":["Documentary","Music","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.3","runtime":"92 min","cast":["Tom Araya","Craig Behrhorst","Pam Behrhorst","Charlie Benante","Marc Biedermann","Chuck Billy","Paul Bostaph","Ray Burton"],"director":["Adam Dubin"],"released":"2019-05-31T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"When only the music mattered...","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Adam Dubin","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/zlV2ROZzeLD4FhnHqUJbASK6DI6.jpg"},{"name":"Tom Araya","c